- Use good Bash script best practices in `.sds/diagnose.sh`: prefer small functions, dispatch into helper scripts when useful, add comments that explain the context of non-obvious checks, and keep the code readable, maintainable, and easy to extend.
- Prefer checks for general live symptoms or invariants such as selector-to-pod matching, missing service endpoints, probe/config references, DNS resolution, dependency reachability, crash loops, or recurring log/error signatures.
- Treat any persistent diagnostic you find or create as a hinting layer. Verify its claims against the live cluster before relying on them.

Start every run with this preflight workflow before broader triage:
